      "content": "I'm currently reviewing the Q3 expense reports for our manufacturing plant in Stuttgart. I've noticed some small, recurring discrepancies in the 'miscellaneous office supplies' ledger. They aren't large enough to trigger a major red flag, but there are these weird, irregular patterns of small amounts being drawn from the budget that don't match any specific purchase orders or standard procurement cycles. \n\nHow can I systematically investigate these types of small-scale, irregular patterns to find the root cause without having to escalate this to a full-scale forensic audit?",
